# V65 · Batch Release Closure

**SSOT:** [TT-V65-BATCH-RELEASE-CLOSURE-LATEST.md](../../docs/runbook/TT-V65-BATCH-RELEASE-CLOSURE-LATEST.md) · [TT-V65-BATCH-RELEASE-CLOSURE-LATEST.json](../../docs/runbook/TT-V65-BATCH-RELEASE-CLOSURE-LATEST.json)

**ACTIVE:** Admin UX / UI / Locale / Dashboard / Workbench 变更走 **Batch Closure**，禁止碎片化上线。  
**Candidate lock:** 工作挂在 **V65** tip / Runtime SSOT 上。**禁止**另起 `V65.1` / `V65.x` 版本轨；Batch 名只是 V65 内收口波次。

## Agent MUST

- Put every non-P0 fix into Gap Inventory → active Batch (current: **V65 Admin UX Batch** · same V65)
- Prefer Daily Release Cut: Audit → Fix → Freeze → one Commit → one Build → one Production Deploy → Runtime Evidence
- Keep batch size in **10–50** items when collecting Admin UX (split modules if 100+)
- After Batch Freeze: verify-only; new findings → next Batch
- Verify `Git` = `Build` = `Deploy` = `Runtime` before claiming Batch CLOSED
- Cite Batch ID + Gap Inventory in handoff notes

## Agent MUST NOT

- Single small fix → immediate Production Deploy (except **P0** incident with explicit Owner scope)
- More than **one** Production Deploy per calendar day for this track (P0 exception)
- Expand scope after Freeze
- Claim Local Batch PASS as Production GO / flip `TT_PRODUCTION_GO`
- Bypass Gap Inventory for Admin UX/UI/Locale/Workbench polish

## P0 exception

Online incident only · separate incident note + Evidence · still record SHA alignment.
